WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.039 --> 00:00:00.872
(fun happy music)

00:00:00.872 --> 00:00:02.300
- [Narrator] Many modern-day fisherman

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:03.930
have a big fish story.

00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:07.643
But in Ancient Japan, the
tiniest fish was the big catch.

00:00:07.643 --> 00:00:11.560
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.867
(moves into dreamy music)

00:00:23.867 --> 00:00:28.110
The art of tanago tsuri is
named after the tanago fish-

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:30.039
one of the smallest fish in the world.

00:00:30.039 --> 00:00:33.956
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:35.571 --> 00:00:39.488
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:47.673
But these special fishing
rods are hard to come by.

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:51.094
That is where Toryo and Shuhei come in.

00:00:51.094 --> 00:00:55.011
(speaking in foreign language)

00:00:58.260 --> 00:00:59.481
The two brothers have been making

00:00:59.481 --> 00:01:03.200
Edo Wazao fishing rods
for the last 15 years

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:05.293
in the hopes of carrying on the tradition.

00:01:05.293 --> 00:01:09.210
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:25.509 --> 00:01:30.132
(moves into funky electronic dance music)

00:01:30.132 --> 00:01:33.324
Each rod can take up to
half a year to finish.

00:01:33.324 --> 00:01:37.241
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:44.509 --> 00:01:46.962
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:46.962 --> 00:01:47.961
(rustling)

00:01:47.961 --> 00:01:50.333
(click)

00:01:50.333 --> 00:01:51.541
(scraping)

00:01:51.541 --> 00:01:53.506
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:53.506 --> 00:01:55.756
(scraping)

00:01:57.010 --> 00:02:00.927
(speaking in foreign language)

00:02:07.426 --> 00:02:09.474
(pleasant orchestral music)

00:02:09.474 --> 00:02:13.391
(speaking in foreign language)

00:02:32.042 --> 00:02:34.459
(sonic beep)

